From: Security Fix <security@example.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Disable JavaScript extraction functions to prevent RCE vulnerability

Disable JavaScript extraction functions to prevent remote code execution.
JavaScript extraction functions can be exploited similarly to filters through
the sampler endpoint and other queries to execute arbitrary system commands.

---
 .../query/extraction/JavaScriptExtractionFn.java | 20 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/processing/src/main/java/org/apache/druid/query/extraction/JavaScriptExtractionFn.java b/processing/src/main/java/org/apache/druid/query/extraction/JavaScriptExtractionFn.java
index 1234567..abcdefg 100644
--- a/processing/src/main/java/org/apache/druid/query/extraction/JavaScriptExtractionFn.java
+++ b/processing/src/main/java/org/apache/druid/query/extraction/JavaScriptExtractionFn.java
@@ -55,6 +55,12 @@ public class JavaScriptExtractionFn implements ExtractionFn
       this.injectedConfig = injectedConfig;
       this.exprType = exprType;

+      // SECURITY FIX: Disable JavaScript extraction functions to prevent RCE
+      if (!injectedConfig.isEnabled()) {
+        throw new IllegalArgumentException(
+            "JavaScript extraction functions are disabled for security reasons. Please use other extraction types.");
+      }
+
       final Context cx = Context.enter();
       try {
         cx.setOptimizationLevel(9);
